{
  "version": 2,
  "date": "2026-11-24",
  "about": "Shared rules for \"Continue on other devices\" (ClearPlay desktop 0.6.0, ClearPlay Android 1.6.0). Desktop runs these in tools/dev-rig/queue-handoff-unit.mjs against src/service/queue-handoff.ts; Android copies this file unchanged and runs the same cases against QueueHandoff.kt. Change this file first, in both apps, when a rule changes. Times are server times (ISO 8601) except nowMs (this device clock, epoch ms). Long lists are written as {\"generate\":{\"prefix\":\"s\",\"from\":A,\"to\":B,\"step\":K}}: the ids s<i> for i = A, A+K, ... while i < B. As songs, each is {\"id\":\"s<i>\",\"local\":false}, except with \"localEvery\":N, where i % N == N-1 is local.",
  "thisApp": {
    "desktop": "ClearPlay",
    "android": "ClearPlay-Android"
  },
  "deviceName": [
    {
      "input": "ClearPlay",
      "expected": "ClearPlay desktop"
    },
    {
      "input": "ClearPlay-Android",
      "expected": "ClearPlay Android"
    },
    {
      "input": "Symfonium",
      "expected": "Symfonium"
    },
    {
      "input": "feishin",
      "expected": "feishin"
    }
  ],
